{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: shipped-state reads are ~68 sequential `gh` downloads per release**

For every unaffected agent (61 of 68 in the rehearsal), `shippedZipManifest` runs its own `gh release download` + `unzip -p`, serially, inside the build loop — plus each pack is now unzipped three times (augment, require gate, validate). Works, but it adds minutes of `gh` round-trips to every release and multiplies the surface for the transient failures comment2.md covers. One batched read would cut both:

